{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/285709-charm-name-spoilers-sidereal-edition","id":285709,"title":"Charm name spoilers: Sidereal edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-17T23:07:34-07:00","id":285709,"title":"Charm name spoilers: Sidereal edition","content":"So, TDO did some tweets.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522938415982317569\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522938415982317569\" target=\"_blank\"> Post </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522938415982317569\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522938415982317569 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This post is from a protected account. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522938577534337024\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522938577534337024\" target=\"_blank\"> Post </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522938577534337024\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522938577534337024 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This post is from a protected account. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522939411764629504\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522939411764629504\" target=\"_blank\"> Post </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522939411764629504\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/RSVance/status/522939411764629504 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This post is from a protected account. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And I like writing Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> INCOME FROM VIRTUE<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 8m (or 4m), 1wp; <b>Mins</b>: Bureaucracy 3, Essence 3; <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Combo-OK<br /> <b>Duration</b>: One project<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Icy Hand<br /> There comes a time when leisure and qualms must be set aside, if duties are to be accomplished promptly. The Sidereal can use this Charm to enhance any project that she is directing or part of, calling on her fellows to uphold the Virtue of her choice. Anyone working on the project may ignore up to (Sidereal\u2019s Bureaucracy) dice of deprivation penalties while doing so. Additionally, their rating in the relevant Virtue is temporarily raised to 3 if it would be lower, and they cannot resist its dictates \u2013 however, they can freely suppress any other Virtues. These effects fade after a break of more than a few minutes, though characters can feel warning pangs before they are struck by the cognitive dissonance or actual (and potentially fatal) penalties.<br /> <br /> Combined, these effects offer the project the benefits of a supporting organizational intimacy (if such an intimacy already exists, the Charm\u2019s mote cost is halved) and the benefits of slave labour with none of the downsides. However, Virtue is only a path, not the destination or end. As a result, workers affected by this Charm must receive material reward for material work. Even bound demons must be promised and receive at least the average wage for the relevant work and region, while dead workers have their wages sent to their family or used as funeral offerings. Failure to pay ends the Charm, and causes those involved to retroactively treat every scene spent working unpaid as one spent building a negative intimacy toward their employer.<br /> <br /> HANDSOME FORTUNE MONEY<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 10m, 1wp; <b>Mins</b>: Craft 4, Essence 3; <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Combo-OK, Shaping, Touch<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: World-Shaping Artistic Vision<br /> A skilled vizier may work the strange economy of destiny like a forge, its heat and hammers provided by strangers both scornful and Samaritan. The Sidereal offers a character who does not recognize him a worthless token he personally created (or extensively modified) in exchange for some good or service. If they accept, the transaction produces a blessing that he may gratefully and openly lay upon them, equivalent to an ascending destiny (<b>Shards of the Exalted Dream</b>, pp. 132). So long as the character bears that token their player may trigger the destiny within, benefiting for a scene. They may do so a number of times equal to the lower of the Resources value of whatever they provided the Sidereal (minimum one) and the Sidereal\u2019s relevant College rating. Characters other than the generous stranger cannot use the token, but can still steal it from them, denying them well-earned good luck.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if the target refuses the Sidereal\u2019s offer, he may openly curse them as a wretch typical of this dying age, shattering the token in their general direction. They suffer this curse as an inauspicious destiny, which activates at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, for a number of scenes equal to the Sidereal\u2019s relevant College rating, less the Resources value of the requested good or service, minimum one.<br /> <br /> A character who would own multiple tokens (or suffer multiple curses) instead immediately loses the one with the fewer remaining uses. Characters cannot be affected by this Charm and an actual astrological destiny at once.<br /> <br /> REGIMENT BETWEEN THE LONELY<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m; <b>Mins</b>: Melee 3, Essence 3; <b>Type</b>: Reflexive (Step 1 for attacks, Step 2 for defence)<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Combo-OK, Knockback<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Harmony of Blows<br /> The Sidereal manipulates the empty spaces in the battlefield\u2019s flow, herding her foes so perfectly that they may mistake a single warrior for a united force somehow outmaneuvering each of them individually. She may activate this Charm in Step 1 of any Melee-based attack she makes or Step 2 of any close range attack made against her, forcing her opponent to move up to (Melee) yards in a direction of her choice as a Knockback effect. They seem to do so of their own volition, and the initial attack is resolved as normal despite the distance; the foe is driven to stumble away by slashes that come from slightly baffling angles, or finds their lunge has somehow led them just a little too far. At the end of Step 10, the Sidereal herself can move the same distance, though she need not move in the same direction. Both types of movement ignore intervening characters who are not actively engaged in a Blockade Movement action.<br /> <br /> Such is the confusion caused by the Sidereal\u2019s maneuvers that even after characters are moved through this Charm, the spot they were standing is treated as occupied for the purposes of being surrounded (<b>Exalted</b>, pp. 155). The Sidereal ignores this effect, and it only lasts for that tick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> hey vance<br /> hurry up and get 3e out<br /> so I can write actual stuff<br /> ffs<br /> this is entirely and exclusively your fault","signature":"","edited":{"userid":605,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","user":"Revlid","date":". 10-19-2014, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T23:38:16-07:00","id":285736,"title":"","content":"Regiment between the Lonely, imagine shouting this in battle, so beautiful, so awesome \u0669(\u0ca5_\u0ca5)\u06f6<br /> <br /> I'll stop making thread that complaining about Sidereal from now on because this just kill all my suspicion on the quality of Ex3 Sidereal (yeah, I'm an easily persuaded person).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T17:58:02-07:00","id":286281,"title":"","content":"Can anyone make out the word on the top of the first picture? Because, until I see the book or am informed otherwise, I intend to assume the charm is called &quot;[something] Income From Virtue Dance&quot;, and the second &quot;Seek Handsome Fortune Money&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T21:32:25-07:00","id":286372,"title":"","content":"Note: the 4 Virtues are thankfully not coming back as discrete mechanical Things in 3e, so there shouldn't be 4 different Income from Virtue Dances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T03:43:33-07:00","id":286554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/285709-charm-name-spoilers-sidereal-edition?p=286372#post286372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: the 4 Virtues are thankfully not coming back as discrete mechanical Things in 3e, so there shouldn't be 4 different Income from Virtue Dances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that these Charms are using Second Edition mechanics. Among other things, you can see keywords relevant to combos and mental influence in use.<br /> <br /> The reasons behind that should be pretty obvious given that Third Edition <i>isn't out yet</i>, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T05:15:40-07:00","id":286566,"title":"","content":"Your write-up for HANDSOME FORTUNE MONEY reminds me a lot of Changeling:The Lost pledges. The Changeling can bestow a boon on someone, so long as they bestow something in return. You could give a boon to a mortal, and they can pay you with resources, which is a lot like this.<br /> <br /> I like this kind of thing for Sidereals, Fate extortion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}